---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Reveal from "../../../components/Reveal.astro";
import { site } from "../../../data/site";

const appName = "Yaniv Score Tracker";
const effectiveDate = "2026-09-29";
const effectiveLabel = "September 29, 2026";
const icon = "/projects/yaniv/app_icon.png";
const ogImage = "/projects/yaniv/og.png";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${appName} Privacy Policy`}
  description="Privacy Policy for Yaniv Score Tracker — what data is stored on device, camera use for QR scanning, AdMob advertising, and Firebase Crashlytics."
  image={ogImage}
  imageAlt={`${appName} app icon`}
  pageType="WebPage"
>
  <article class="page-container page-section max-w-3xl">
    <Reveal>
      <header class="border-b border-border/60 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <img
            src={icon}
            alt={`${appName} icon`}
            width={72}
            height={72}
            class="h-16 w-16 shrink-0 rounded-2xl bg-surface-raised object-contain ring-1 ring-border sm:h-[4.5rem] sm:w-[4.5rem]"
          />
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ruby">Legal</p>
            <h1 class="font-serif mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
              Privacy Policy
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base font-medium text-accent">{appName}</p>
            <time datetime={effectiveDate} class="mt-3 block text-sm text-muted">
              Effective date: {effectiveLabel}
            </time>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>
    </Reveal>

    <Reveal delay={60}>
      <div class="legal-content mt-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          {appName} (“the App,” “we,” or “us”) values your privacy. This policy explains what
          information is handled when you use the App on iOS, Android, and other supported
          platforms, and how that information is used.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using the App, you agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do not
          use the App.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Handle</h2>

        <h3>1.1 Data you enter (stored on your device)</h3>
        <p>The App stores on your device:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Player names you enter</li>
          <li>Round scores and totals</li>
          <li>Game settings and history you generate while playing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This gameplay data is saved locally (for example via on-device storage).
          <strong>
            We do not operate our own servers that receive your player names or score history.
          </strong>
        </p>

        <h3>1.2 Device permissions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Camera:</strong> Used only when you choose to scan a game QR code shared from
            another device. Camera frames are processed on device for scanning. We do not upload
            photos or video from the camera to our servers. You can deny camera access; core score
            tracking still works without it.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1.3 Data collected by third-party services</h3>
        <p>
          The App uses third-party software development kits (SDKs) that may collect information as
          described below. We do not control those services’ independent processing once data is
          sent to them.
        </p>

        <h3>Google AdMob (advertising)</h3>
        <p>
          The App displays ads through Google AdMob. AdMob and its partners may collect or receive
          information such as:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Advertising identifiers (for example Apple’s IDFA or Android’s Advertising ID), subject
            to your device and OS settings
          </li>
          <li>Device and app information (device model, OS version, app version, language)</li>
          <li>IP address and approximate location derived from it</li>
          <li>Ad interaction data (views, clicks)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is used to serve and measure ads, and may be used for personalized
          advertising where allowed. On iOS, cross-app tracking for advertising is subject to
          Apple’s App Tracking Transparency rules and your choice if the system asks for
          permission. You can also limit ad tracking in your device settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google’s advertising privacy information:
          <br />
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads
          </a>
          <br />
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            https://policies.google.com/privacy
          </a>
        </p>

        <h3>Firebase Crashlytics (crash reporting)</h3>
        <p>
          In release builds, the App uses Firebase Crashlytics (Google) to collect crash and
          stability reports so we can fix bugs. This may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Crash logs and stack traces</li>
          <li>Device model, OS version, and app version</li>
          <li>Approximate diagnostic information about the state of the App at the time of a crash</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Crashlytics is used to improve App stability. It is not used to serve ads.</p>
        <p>
          Firebase / Google privacy information:
          <br />
          <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy
          </a>
          <br />
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            https://policies.google.com/privacy
          </a>
        </p>

        <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Local gameplay data</strong> is used only to run the App for you: tracking
            scores, applying rules, showing history, and sharing a game state via QR between
            devices you control.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Ads</strong> support the App at no purchase cost.</li>
          <li><strong>Crash reports</strong> help us diagnose and fix crashes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell your player names or score history. Advertising partners may process
          device and ad-related data under their own policies as part of showing ads.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Data Storage and Deletion</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Player names, scores, and history remain on your device unless you delete them by
            clearing the App’s storage or uninstalling the App.
          </li>
          <li>
            Crash and advertising data processed by Google are retained according to Google’s
            policies and retention periods.
          </li>
          <li>
            QR game sharing transfers game state between devices via codes you scan; it does not
            upload that state to our servers.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Children’s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The App is a general-audience score tracker and is
          <strong>not directed at children under 13</strong>
          (or the equivalent minimum age in your region). We do not knowingly collect personal
          information from children for our own accounts or profiles. Because the App includes
          third-party advertising, parents and guardians should supervise use by minors and review
          device ad and privacy settings.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your Choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Camera:</strong> Grant or deny in system Settings; scanning is optional.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Ads / tracking:</strong> Use platform settings (for example Limit Ad Tracking /
            App Tracking Transparency on iOS, or Google ad settings on Android) to control
            advertising identifiers and personalized ads where available.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Local data:</strong> Uninstall the App or clear App storage to remove locally
            saved names, scores, and history.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact:</strong> Email us (below) with privacy questions or deletion-related
            requests we can reasonably address for data we control.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. International Processing</h2>
        <p>
          Third-party providers such as Google may process data in the United States or other
          countries where they operate. Where required by law, those transfers are governed by the
          providers’ contractual and privacy safeguards.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy when the App’s features or legal requirements change.
          The updated policy will show a new effective date. Continued use of the App after an
          update means you accept the revised policy.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about this policy, contact:</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Email:</strong>{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </Reveal>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .legal-content h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .legal-content h3 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .legal-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-content ul,
  .legal-content ol {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .legal-content ol {
    list-style: decimal;
  }

  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--color-ruby);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .legal-content a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
